{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["As for me, when I came from Paddan — on that journey, after the Holy One, blessed be He, had blessed me, Rachel died on that road, with still a long way to go before any settlement; therefore I buried her on the road, for there was no time to bury her beside Leah in the Cave of Machpelah. And lest Yosef be distressed about his mother, he needed to say this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The verb ושלא יפשיעהו (literally 'and so that he not cause him to cease/mourn') is textually uncertain; rendered here as 'lest Yosef be distressed,' understanding the subject as Yaakov explaining to Yosef why he tells him this."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:29.818682764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}